      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 58-year-old male patient was referred to the dermatologist because of swelling and pain of his left ankle. Radiodiagnostic imaging revealed an osteodestructive tumor which after biopsy proved to be a chondrosarcoma. Malignancy should be in the differential diagnosis of chronic one-sided edema."},
